ion":1,"reason":null,"unit_id":"agent:E4","usage":{"input_tokens":193758,"output_tokens":4378,"requests":8}}],"version":1},"findings":[{"block_threshold":0.75,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Correct the 'Why' call-chain: the per-mutation `_recheck_drift`/`snapshot_head` (git rev-parse) fires in the apply loop at `applier.py:639` immediately before `_apply_one` (line 640), not from inside `_apply_one` (which does not call it).","cohort":["E4"],"criteria":["E4"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.0056,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["applier.py:639 `head_pin_cell[0] = _recheck_drift(concurrency, repo_root, head_pin_cell[0])` then line 640 `_apply_one(mutation, ctx, mutations_with_outcomes)` — _recheck_drift is called in the loop, before _apply_one","_apply_one body (applier.py:677-706) calls _audit_rebar_id_label_writes and dispatch_mutation, never _recheck_drift","applier_drift_guard.py:100 `_recheck_drift` -> `concurrency.snapshot_head(repo_root)`; _concurrency.py:30 -> git_adapter.rev_parse (git rev-parse subprocess) — the downstream chain is correct"],"finding":"The 'Why' attributes the per-mutation git rev-parse to _apply_one ('_apply_one, which calls _recheck_drift'), but _apply_one (applier.py:677-706) does not call _recheck_drift; the per-mutation apply loop invokes _recheck_drift on applier.py:639 immediately BEFORE calling _apply_one on line 640. The substantive claim (one git rev-parse subprocess per mutation, one RECON line, one outcome record) is verified and holds, but the call-chain attribution is mechanically wrong.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f377b3ba1fdd89dfb","impact":0.85,"is_primary":null,"location":"Why section: 'Each inert mutation still traverses `_apply_one`, which calls `_recheck_drift` -> `concurrency.snapshot_head(repo_root)`'","norm_id":"nbf1c089f06ac8eae","priority":0.7556,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A reader/implementer tracing the cost path to confirm the skip removes the git rev-parse follows _apply_one and finds no _recheck_drift call there, undermining confidence in the rationale."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Reword to: 'Each inert mutation still drives one per-mutation loop iteration in the batch apply path (applier.py:639-640), which calls `_recheck_drift` -> `concurrency.snapshot_head(repo_root)` — a `git rev-parse` subprocess — before dispatching via `_apply_one`.'","tier":"LLM","validity":0.8889,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"contradicts_reality","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Spell out the causal chain from a NON-empty resolved `changed` to an empty effective outbound payload (why `if changed:` at differ.py:598 passes yet the row is inert), since `_mutation_to_batch_dict` copies `changed_fields` verbatim — otherwise the proposed skip predicate may never fire.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.4,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["differ.py:598 `if changed:` is the sole gate on the branch-3 `_emit`","batch_dispatch.py:191-195: update path sets `fields = dict(raw_changed_fields)` with no per-field filtering, so non-empty changed_fields => non-empty fields","Plan: 'skip the branch-3 `_emit` only when the resolved `changed` dict contains no field that survives `_mutation_to_batch_dict`'","Plan Why: '~516 mutations per pass that are provably inert' — but an empty `changed` already does not emit today"],"finding":"The plan's inertness predicate ('resolved `changed` contains no field that survives `_mutation_to_batch_dict`') does not obviously match the mechanism by which branch-3 emits: differ.py:598 already gates emit on `if changed:`, and `_mutation_to_batch_dict` (batch_dispatch.py:189-195) copies `changed_fields` verbatim without dropping fields — so a non-empty `changed` never yields an empty `fields`, and an empty `changed` never reaches emit. The plan must state HOW a non-empty resolved `changed` becomes an empty effective payload (e.g. conflict_resolver.resolve_field returning the jira value so the diff is a Jira-side no-op), or the proposed skip predicate will never fire on the ~516 rows.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f77bad69c98814152","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach paragraph + Why paragraph","norm_id":"n85007d4f812b79cb","priority":1.0,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Implementer adds a post-resolution check `if _mutation_to_batch_dict(...).get('fields'):` and finds it is always truthy for the emitting rows, so 0 mutations are skipped and AC1 fails"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisit